  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "**This is the hard version of the problem. It is worth 757575 points in division 111, 100100100 points in division 222, and is not scored in all other divisions.**\n\nFor an array BBB of length MMM, you are allowed to perform the following operation as many times as required:\n\n\nLet S=∑i=1MBiS = \\sum\\limits_{i=1}^M{B_i}S=i=1∑M​Bi​\nPick iii such that 1≤i≤min⁡(M,∣S∣)1 \\leq i \\leq \\min(M,|S|)1≤i≤min(M,∣S∣)\nEither increment or decrement BiB_iBi​ by 111\nDefine f(B)f(B)f(B) to be the minimum number of operations needed to turn every element of BBB to 000, or −1-1−1 if it's impossible to achieve.\n\nYou are given an array AAA of length NNN and QQQ queries.\n\nFor each query, given LiL_iLi​ and RiR_iRi​, output the value of f(A[Li…Ri])f(A[L_i\\ldots R_i])f(A[Li​…Ri​]), where A[Li…Ri]A[L_i\\ldots R_i]A[Li​…Ri​] represents the subarray of AAA from the LiL_iLi​-th index to the RiR_iRi​-th index, that is, [ALi,ALi+1,…,ARi][A_{L_i}, A_{L_i + 1}, \\ldots, A_{R_i}][ALi​​,ALi​+1​,…,ARi​​].\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains two space-separated integers NNN and QQQ — the number of elements of the array AAA and the number of queries, respectively.\nThe second line of each test case contains NNN space-separated integers — the elements of the array AAA.\nThe next QQQ lines describe the queries. The iii-th of these QQQ lines contains two space-separated integers LiL_iLi​ and RiR_iRi​ — the subarray that needs to be considered for the iii-th query.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each query, output on a new line the value of f(A[Li…Ri])f(A[L_i\\ldots R_i])f(A[Li​…Ri​]).",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "1≤N≤2⋅1051 \\leq N \\leq 2\\cdot10^51≤N≤2⋅105",
      "1≤Q≤2⋅1051 \\leq Q \\leq 2\\cdot10^51≤Q≤2⋅105",
      "−109≤Ai≤109-10^9 \\leq A_i \\leq 10^9−109≤Ai​≤109",
      "1≤Li≤Ri≤N1 \\leq L_i \\leq R_i \\leq N1≤Li​≤Ri​≤N",
      "The sum of NNN and the sum of QQQ over all test cases won't exceed 2⋅1052\\cdot10^52⋅105."
